CM_ BO_ 168 "c_FSJB_DoorStatus_0x0A8: door/bonnet/trunk status INPUT the cluster consumes (from FSJB). Present in candump-2026-07-16_213719.log (late MY XF250). BENCH-CONFIRMED 2026-08-16 (validate_door_causation.py): driving this frame with byte5=0x3F then 0x3E made the cluster's HS output 0x337 byte2 follow (0x3F -> 0x3E), proving byte5 is the door mask and bit0 = Front-Left. Minimal accepted payload: byte0=0x80 (validity gate), byte2=0x10 (bong disable), byte5=door mask (bit0 FL, 0x3F=all closed).";
CM_ BO_ 472 "c_MS_IPC_ClockCounterMirror_0x1D8: BENCH-CONFIRMED 2026-08-16 (validate_clock_counter.py). Bytes 4-7 are a 32-bit big-endian counter; pre-wake FF FF FF FF. It is the SAME counter, in lock-step, as HS 0x4FF (c_HS_IPC_RTCTimestamp) -- both started at 0x5C0BEDC4 and incremented together. Rate ~10 Hz (increment every ~100ms), measured 9.99/s here vs 10.01/s on 0x4FF -- NOT a 1 Hz seconds clock. The magnitude on the bench (0x5C0B..) resembles a Dec-2018 unix value, but the 2015MF candump-2026-07-16_213719.log has a DIFFERENT cluster reading 0x9C844D74 (~year 2053 if read as epoch) at the same 9.99/s rate -- so the date-resemblance is coincidental and it is definitively NOT unix seconds; it is a free-running counter. CROSS-REVISION VALIDATED on the 2015MF cluster (same s/w family, next revision): 0x1D8 bytes 4-7 = 32-bit BE counter at 9.99/s there too. byte0 bit6 (0x40) toggles per frame like 0x188. Cluster-owned output. SPEED HYPOTHESIS REJECTED 2026-08-16 (search_speed_mirror_ms.py): the 2007MY Rhys decode read bytes 1-2 as speed*0.0065; injecting HS 0x20B speed (needle+LCD tracked correctly) left 0x1D8 bytes 1-2 fixed at 0x0000 -- speed is mirrored on 0x028 b6-7 instead, not here.";
CM_ BO_ 392 "c_MS_IPC_Odometer_0x188: BENCH-CONFIRMED 2026-08-16 (validate_odometer_frames.py). Bytes 4-6 (24-bit LE) = odometer raw; observed 0xD74C0A, identical to 0x388 bytes 5-7 in the same run (the two odometer frames cross-agree). byte0 bit6 (0x40) alternates every frame (i_AliveToggle_b0) -- confirmed as a per-frame toggle; whether it is alive/parity vs an odometer-update strobe is i_ (odometer was static so no update event to correlate).";
CM_ BO_ 904 "c_MS_IPC_Odometer_0x388: BENCH-CONFIRMED 2026-08-16 (validate_odometer_frames.py). Bytes 5-7 (24-bit LE) = odometer raw; observed 0xD74C0A, identical to 0x188 bytes 4-6 -- the two odometer frames cross-agree.";
CM_ BO_ 888 "c_MS_IPC_ClockMinSec_0x378: cluster time output. bytes 6-7 = MM:SS -- byte7 = seconds (ticks +1/sec, wraps at 60), byte6 = minutes (increments when seconds wrap). i_: byte7 as a ~1Hz counter is bench-observed (MY2014 IPC-only PowerOn capture, byte7 0->4 with byte6=0 fresh); the MM:SS wall-clock meaning is corroborated by the 2015MF candump-2026-07-16_213719.log (byte6:byte7 = 43:55 climbing, byte7 wraps 0x3b->00 lifting byte6). Same MM:SS value appears in 0x4E9 in lock-step. NOT synced to real wall time in either capture (free-running RTC) -- the RTC is set by a separate sporadic ICP 'Set time' event frame, not seen in cyclic dumps.";
CM_ BO_ 1257 "c_MS_IPC_ClockMinSec_0x4E9: cluster time output carrying the SAME MM:SS as 0x378 (bytes 6-7, byte7=seconds wraps at 60, byte6=minutes), plus byte0=0x80, byte1 fixed. Same evidence/caveats as 0x378. i_.";

CM_ BO_ 360 "c_MS_IPC_TurnIndicatorRequest_0x168: IPC-TRANSMITTED (TX by the cluster on MS). Turn-indicator REQUEST sent to the CJB, derived from the analog Direction-Indicator resistor-ladder switch on cluster pin C2LF27/1 (with SW_RET return). byte0 = decoded DI switch state; it changes across 0x08-0x0C as the DI-line resistance changes. BENCH-CONFIRMED: ~1kR = OFF (0x08), ~220R = LEFT (0x0A), open-circuit = 0x0B. RIGHT (470R) and short states not yet captured but expected within the 0x08-0x0C range. Bytes 1-7 static in captures (example: 08 00 00 FF FF 00 7B FF). Firmware: DI decode is threshold descriptor sid 0x04 (ADC thresholds 328/616/728/868 -> 5 states short/LEFT/OFF/RIGHT/open); an unwired stalk floats to the open band, which also sets DTC 9D3615 'Turn indicator open circuit'. NOTE: this is the cluster's turn-switch READING output; the green turn TELLTALES themselves are flashed by RJB/RSJB ON/OFF timing (0x048/0x068), and hazards are commanded by the CJB (both arrows).";
CM_ SG_ 360 c_TurnSwitchState "byte0 decoded Direction-Indicator switch state. Confirmed: 0x08=OFF(~1kR), 0x0A=LEFT(~220R), 0x0B=open. Full observed range 0x08-0x0C; RIGHT(470R)/short unconfirmed.";

VAL_ 136 c_PowerMode 0 "IgnitionOff" 4 "Accessory" 6 "IgnitionOn" 7 "EngineRunning" 9 "EngineCranking" ;
VAL_ 360 c_TurnSwitchState 8 "OFF_Neutral" 10 "LEFT" 11 "OpenCircuit_Fault" ;